WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.360
We all want to eat
the kinds of foods

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:05.280
that make us feel
better and live longer.

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:08.400
But there’s so much conflicting
information out there,

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.920
so many nutrition opinions.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:14.100
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast,

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:15.900
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:18.600
It’s my job to give you
the information you need

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.000
to make the healthiest
choices possible.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.500
Kidney disease ranks as the 9th
leading cause of death in the U.S.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.160
So what foods should we eat
to keep our kidneys healthy?

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:30.540
Here’s our first story.

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:34.080
Chronic kidney disease is one
of the top ten leading causes

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.300
of premature death
in the United States,

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.700
and its incidence
is increasing.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:41.460
Chronic kidney disease
affects more than 10 percent

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:43.680
of the adult population,
and each year,

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:47.700
more than 100,000 Americans
develop end-stage kidney disease

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:49.320
and have to go on dialysis.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:53.520
What’s crazy is that a staggering
96 percent of individuals

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:56.100
with mild to moderate
decreases in kidney function

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.560
and about half
of individuals with severely

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:01.080
decreased kidney function
go undiagnosed.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:02.400
Meaning the vast majority,

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.460
like 24 out of 25 people
with chronic kidney disease,

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:07.680
don’t even know
they have it.

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.220
What can we do to maintain
our kidney function?

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:13.860
Well, in a study that followed
more than a thousand older women

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:16.560
for a decade, those consuming
a diet that is richer

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:20.160
in plant-based protein had a slower
decline in kidney function,

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:23.580
extending support for the health
benefits of plant-rich diets

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:26.280
in the general population
to maintain kidney health.

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:29.460
Compared with protein
from plant sources,

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:32.040
animal protein has been associated
with an increased risk

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:34.680
of end-stage kidney disease
in several such studies.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:36.420
We’re not exactly sure why.

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:39.300
Kidney damage from animal
protein could result

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:42.720
from the dietary acid load,
excess phosphorus,

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:46.740
or gut microbiome bad bacteria
and the resultant inflammation.

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:50.820
The dietary acid load in a Standard
American Diet is derived

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:54.660
mostly from animal sources
such as meats, eggs, and cheeses.

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:57.660
In contrast, by including
a higher proportion of foods

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:00.840
with natural alkali,
such as fruits and vegetables,

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:04.080
a strictly plant-based diet
is nearly acid neutral.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:06.720
Even just eating plant-based
2 or 3 days a week

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:09.240
can significantly
bring down the acid load

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:12.120
delivered to the kidneys,
and eat plant-based full time,

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:14.940
and you can actually flip
over into alkaline territory.

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:18.780
Even just cutting out meat
can yield an alkaline load

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:21.840
compared to the acid
load in the nonvegetarians.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:25.380
All this is important,
since dietary acid may promote

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:28.860
kidney injury and a progressive
decline in kidney function.

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:32.640
The intake of animal protein
can also cause an imbalance

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:35.520
in the composition of the gut
microbiome by producing

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:38.520
more ammonia and the rotten
egg gas hydrogen sulfide,

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:41.280
and have a proinflammatory
effect that may result

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:43.260
in reduced kidney function,

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:46.440
but it also may be
the animal fat.

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:48.420
In the Harvard Nurses Study,

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:51.060
higher intake of animal fat
was directly associated

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:53.040
with the loss of protein
in the urine,

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:55.080
which is a sign
of kidney damage,

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:58.080
and to protect against that,
they suggest diets lower

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:01.260
in animal protein,
animal fat, and cholesterol.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:04.020
That may help
explain why vegetarians

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:06.840
have better kidney function
than nonvegetarians

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:08.700
matched for sex, age, size,

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:10.920
physical activity, alcohol, smoking, etc.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:15.060
So effectively, even a meat eater
who is just as slim as a vegetarian,

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:17.340
just as healthy cholesterol,
blood pressure,

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:22.020
and blood sugar control-wise
still had inferior kidney function.

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:25.500
They think it might be
the higher dietary fiber intake

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:27.480
on more plant-based
diets contributing

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:29.760
to the protective effect
on kidney function,

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:32.160
again through
a microbiome mechanism.

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:34.800
Whereas the consumption
of animal protein may lead

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:36.780
to a proliferation
of meat-eating bugs,

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:39.840
which can result in a
leaky gut, uremic toxins,

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:42.300
and resulting inflammation,
oxidative stress,

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:44.040
and chronic kidney
disease progression.

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:47.880
That can be blocked, with
the decreased inflammation

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:52.020
and acid load thanks to the
eating of more fiber rich foods.

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:55.800
No wonder an egg-free
vegetarian dietary pattern

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:58.920
was associated with a 37 percent
decreased odds

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.600
of developing chronic
kidney disease.

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:04.260
But, what about plant-based diets
for not just the prevention

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:07.080
but the management
of chronic kidney disease?

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:09.600
Can comprehensive
lifestyle change alter

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:11.400
the course of chronic
kidney disease?

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:14.340
This was the case report
of someone diagnosed

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:16.260
with minimal
changes disease.

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:19.560
That’s when someone’s kidneys
start leaking protein,

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:21.600
even though there
are minimal changes seen

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:23.460
in biopsies under
the microscope.

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:26.700
You give people steroids,
and in a few months,

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:29.220
you can knock it down,
but a significant fraction

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:31.920
may fail to respond
to the steroid therapy.

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:34.440
He was diagnosed
18 years prior,

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:37.860
but only by replacing animal
protein with plant-based protein

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:39.600
was he able
to put his chronic

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:41.400
kidney disease
into remission.

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:45.840
At age 44, he suddenly developed
swelling that crept up

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:48.480
throughout his body since
he was losing so much protein.

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:51.000
He was weak, unable
to concentrate, and lethargic.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:53.700
Diagnosed with
minimal change disease

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:55.080
and treated with a water pill

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:57.840
and four different blood
pressure lowering agents.

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:01.500
Because of unresponsiveness
to high-dose steroids,

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:03.660
a powerful immunosuppressant
was added;

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:06.180
yet, severe protein
loss continued

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:09.180
and his hypertension and
kidney function worsened

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:12.540
until...he started eating
plant-based,

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:15.060
started exercising,
lost 60 pounds,

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:18.780
and his kidney disease
went away and stayed away.

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:21.480
Let’s hear it
in his own words.

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:25.020
“I appreciate the recommendations
my doctor gave me

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:26.760
about making
dietary modifications:

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:29.880
‘replace your protein intake
with plant-based protein.’

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:33.900
This one change has had
a monumental impact on my life.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:37.740
I have gained back a quality of life
that I thought was gone forever.

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:41.520
My benchmark for normal
has been my ability to keep up

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:44.640
with my professional work demands
and still be able to exercise.

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:48.420
For the last 7 months, I now swim
over three miles every other day:

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:51.360
a distance that surpasses
my pre–kidney disease life.

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:55.440
I perceived I lived a healthy
lifestyle before kidney disease;

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:58.440
today, I live a healthier,
happier lifestyle,

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:01.820
and I have my kidneys
to thank for it.

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:03.660
In our next story,

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:08.760
we look at the significant dietary risk
factors for declining kidney function.

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:14.220
Kidney failure may be both prevented
and treated with a plant-based diet,

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:18.960
and no wonder; kidneys are
highly vascular organs.

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:22.260
Harvard researchers found three
significant dietary risk factors

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:27.900
for declining kidney function: animal
protein, animal fat, and cholesterol.

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:33.060
Animal fat can alter the actual structure
of our kidneys, based on studies like this,

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:37.380
showing plugs of fat literally clogging up
the works in autopsied human kidneys.

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:39.840
And the animal protein can
have a profound effect

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:43.380
on normal kidney function,
inducing what's called hyperfiltration,

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:47.280
increasing the workload of
the kidney; but not plant protein.

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:51.300
Eat a meal of tuna fish and you can see
the increased pressure on the kidneys

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:56.280
go up within 1, 2, 3 hours after the meal,
in both nondiabetics and diabetics.

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:59.460
So we're not talking adverse
effects decades down the road,

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:02.340
but literally within hours
of it going into our mouth.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:06.660
Now, if instead of having a tuna
salad sandwich, though,

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:09.180
you had a tofu salad sandwich,

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:11.580
with the exact same amount
of protein, what happens?

00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:13.260
No effect.

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:16.680
Dealing with plant protein
is no problem.

00:07:16.680 --> 00:07:21.540
Why does animal protein cause the
overload reaction, but not plant protein?

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:25.080
It appears to be due to
the inflammation triggered

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:26.760
by the consumption
of animal products.

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:28.080
How do we know that?

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:31.080
Because, if you give a powerful,
anti-inflammatory drug

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:34.560
along with that tuna fish, you
can abolish the hyperfiltration,

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:37.320
protein leakage response
to meat ingestion.

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:41.400
Then, there's the acid load.

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:46.080
Animal foods—meat, eggs, and dairy—
induce the formation of acid

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:49.800
within the kidneys, which
may lead to tubular toxicity,

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:53.160
damage to the tiny, delicate,
urine-making tubes in the kidney.

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:59.280
Animal foods tend to be acid forming—
especially fish, which is the worst—

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:00.360
then pork and poultry,

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:03.240
whereas plant foods tend
to be relatively neutral,

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:07.140
or actually alkaline, base-forming
to counteract the acid.

00:08:07.140 --> 00:08:10.200
So the key to halting the progression
of chronic kidney disease

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:15.496
might be in the produce market,
rather than the pharmacy.

00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:17.340
Finally today,

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:20.700
I share a touching story of the
power of plant-based eating

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:22.260
for chronic kidney failure.

00:08:22.260 --> 00:08:25.560
Is it possible to ameliorate
chronic kidney disease

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:27.180
using a whole food,
plant-based diet?

00:08:27.180 --> 00:08:29.460
In my last video
on kidney disease,

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:32.220
I talked about how randomizing
people to cut just around

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:35.880
10 grams of protein from their
daily diet could cut their risk

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:39.000
of dialysis and death
by a whopping 77%.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:42.660
That was cutting protein
across the board.

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:46.080
But while animal-based
protein ingestion —

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:48.300
meat, dairy, and egg white
protein ingestion —

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:51.540
promotes an acidic environment
in the kidneys, inflammation, and

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:54.300
stresses the kidneys to what's
called hyperfiltration mode,

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:57.900
plant-based protein can be
alkaline-producing and

00:08:57.900 --> 00:09:00.780
anti-inflammatory and contain
kidney-protective properties.

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:05.280
So, what if you have kidney patients
eat a plant-dominant low-protein diet,

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:11.040
abbreviated adorably as PLADO,
I guess for plant-dominant.

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:15.000
If you fashion up a plant-based diet
index score where you get points

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:16.080
for healthy plant foods

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:18.600
and get points deducted
for eating animal foods,

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:21.900
those with serious kidney disease
with higher scores were found

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:23.820
to have lower systemic inflammation.

00:09:23.820 --> 00:09:27.420
But does that actually translate
into living a longer life?

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:28.800
Apparently so.

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:32.340
Even a 10% increase in the
proportion of plant-based protein

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:36.240
was associated with a significant
reduction in all-cause mortality.

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:39.960
Even just eating more servings of
fruits and vegetables, like two a day

00:09:39.960 --> 00:09:43.200
compared to two a week,
is linked to living longer.

00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:46.620
Without fully functioning kidneys,

00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:50.160
there are concerns about
phosphorus and potassium overload,

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:51.660
though, on a plant-based diet.

00:09:51.660 --> 00:09:55.620
But the phosphorus in plant-based
foods is not as much of a problem

00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:58.860
as the phosphorus additives
in processed and animal foods.

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:02.280
And the risk of potassium overload
from plant-based diets appears

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:04.620
overstated and not supported
by the evidence.

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:09.000
But you don't know about
ameliorating chronic kidney disease

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:13.620
using a whole food, plant-based
diet until you put it to the test.

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:17.100
Here's a case report of a 69-year-old
man with type 2 diabetes,

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:20.580
high blood pressure, and
stage 3 chronic kidney disease,

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:24.120
resulting in elevated phosphorus
and potassium in the blood,

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:28.320
Interested in changing his diet
to improve his medical condition.

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:30.840
That's my kind of patient!

00:10:30.840 --> 00:10:35.340
He was on 12 different medications,
eating a diet that may actually be

00:10:35.340 --> 00:10:37.320
slightly better than
the average American:

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:39.120
some whole grains and beans,

00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:42.960
but then his doctor advised to try
eating whole food, plant-based.

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:46.860
So, oatmeal with fruit and flax,
beans and greens,

00:10:46.860 --> 00:10:49.740
whole wheat spaghetti and
veggies, fruit as snacks.

00:10:49.740 --> 00:10:53.220
Counselled to eat as much as he
wanted from whole healthy foods;

00:10:53.220 --> 00:10:57.210
no carb counting, no calorie counting,
no portion size restriction —

00:10:57.210 --> 00:11:01.200
improving the quality of food rather
than restricting the quantity of food.

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:04.800
He adopted the whole food,
plant-based diet, packed with carbs,

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:08.820
yet rapidly reduced his insulin
requirements by more than 50%,

00:11:08.820 --> 00:11:11.340
and subsequently saw
improvements in weight,

00:11:11.340 --> 00:11:13.320
blood pressure,
and cholesterol.

00:11:13.320 --> 00:11:16.020
Because eating healthy
can have such a rapid effect

00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:18.300
on improving your body's
insulin sensitivity,

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:21.120
immediate adjustments
in insulin dosing were made.

00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:24.540
Within four days, his insulin dose
was able to be reduced

00:11:24.540 --> 00:11:28.620
from roughly 210 units of insulin
a day down to 70 units daily,

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:31.860
and an oral blood-sugar lowering
medication had to be stopped

00:11:31.860 --> 00:11:33.960
due to rapidly improving blood sugar.

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:38.460
He also was able to stop his
carvedilol, the hydrochlorothiazide,

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:41.760
amlodipine, sitagliptin
within the first two months

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:43.800
due to improving blood pressure
and blood sugars.

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:46.680
His insulin dose was
steadily titrated downward.

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:51.120
His pravastatin dose was cut in half,
and he lost about 50 pounds.

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:55.200
Okay, so what happened
to his stage 3 kidney failure?

00:11:55.200 --> 00:11:58.661
He was no longer in
stage 3 kidney failure!

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:02.820
He experienced an increase
in estimated GFR of 73%,

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:05.460
suggesting that the improvement
in estimated kidney function

00:12:05.460 --> 00:12:08.100
was greater than what would be
expected from weight loss alone.

00:12:08.100 --> 00:12:11.820
For example, lose about 60 pounds
from bariatric surgery,

00:12:11.820 --> 00:12:14.520
and you only get
about a 12 to 15% boost.

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:18.420
Bottom line: for individuals
with chronic kidney disease,

00:12:18.420 --> 00:12:21.660
especially those with obesity,
hypertension, or diabetes,

00:12:21.660 --> 00:12:24.780
a strict, all-you-care-to-eat
whole food, plant-based diet

00:12:24.780 --> 00:12:26.700
may confer significant benefit.

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:30.300
I mean, apart from the
kidney-specific outcomes,

00:12:30.300 --> 00:12:34.140
overall mortality is significantly
lower among kidney patients

00:12:34.140 --> 00:12:35.460
who eat more plants.

00:12:35.460 --> 00:12:39.180
And that's critical because most
kidney patients don't even make it

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:41.880
to dialysis because they die first,

00:12:41.880 --> 00:12:44.940
most often from
cardiovascular disease.

00:12:45.540 --> 00:12:47.760
Let's hear from the patient.

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:51.540
"At the outset, it seemed like
this was going to be a difficult

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:52.680
and restrictive way to eat,

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:55.770
but I began feeling different
almost immediately

00:12:55.770 --> 00:12:59.160
and we had to decrease
my insulin after ONE day.

00:12:59.160 --> 00:13:03.000
It seemed like almost overnight I had
more energy than I'd had in years.

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:07.020
Weight I'd been trying to lose for
a decade began dropping off.

00:13:07.020 --> 00:13:10.620
As the weight came off, I felt lighter,
and more able to move my body again.

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:16.320
This lifestyle change has been
the greatest gift I've ever received.

00:13:16.320 --> 00:13:20.220
I am off most of my medications,
I've lost over 70 pounds,

00:13:20.220 --> 00:13:23.460
and I've regained control
over my health.

00:13:23.460 --> 00:13:26.040
I feel empowered
by this lifestyle change,

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:28.740
and I finally feel like I'm
in charge of my health,

00:13:29.340 --> 00:13:33.600
not just an unlucky victim shuffling
from one specialist to the next.

00:13:34.380 --> 00:13:39.325
My only regret was that
I didn't know about this sooner."

00:13:40.865 --> 00:13:43.260
We would love it if you could
share with us your stories

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:46.020
about reinventing your health
through evidence-based nutrition.

00:13:46.020 --> 00:13:48.900
Go to nutritionfacts.org/testimonials.

00:13:48.900 --> 00:13:52.440
We may share it on our social
media to help inspire others.

00:13:54.420 --> 00:13:58.500
To see any graphs, charts, graphics,
images, or studies mentioned here,

00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:01.080
go to the NutritionFacts
Podcast landing page.

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:03.360
There you’ll find all the
detailed information you need –

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:07.200
plus, links to all of the sources
we cite for each of these topics.

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:10.980
My last two books are
“How to Survive a Pandemic”

00:14:10.980 --> 00:14:13.080
and my “How Not to Diet Cookbook”.

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:16.380
Get ready this year for the
launch of How Not to Age.

00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:18.840
And, of course, all the proceeds
I receive from the sales

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:21.180
of all my books goes
directly to charity.

00:14:21.180 --> 00:14:24.960
NutritionFacts.org is a nonprofit,
science-based public service,

00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:26.640
where you can sign up
for free daily updates

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:30.660
on the latest in nutrition research
with bite-sized videos and articles

00:14:30.660 --> 00:14:32.820
uploaded nearly every day.

00:14:33.420 --> 00:14:35.340
Everything on the
website is free.

00:14:35.340 --> 00:14:37.620
There’s no ads, no
corporate sponsorships,

00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:38.400
no kickbacks.

00:14:38.400 --> 00:14:40.500
It’s strictly non-commercial.
I’m not selling anything.

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:44.100
I just put it up as a public service,
as a labor of love,

00:14:44.100 --> 00:14:46.380
as a tribute to
my grandmother,

00:14:46.380 --> 00:14:50.872
whose own life was saved
with evidence-based nutrition.

